%% DM26-0670

%% A client connects and registers, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md, "The flows" and "What is
%% refused"). What supersede does is broker/session_supersede_takeover, and coming back is broker/client_reconnect.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (the client's transport)
    participant LM as ListenerManager
    participant Listener
    participant Broker
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgent

    Client->>LM: TCP connect, mutual TLS (the cluster's CA)
    LM->>Listener: spawn, one per connection
    Listener->>Listener: from the leaf: identity (first DNS SAN), serial,<br/>floor (p:pub, p:sub), instance (i:uid, i:pod)
    Client->>Listener: RegistrationRequest(protocol, registration_id or none)

    alt another protocol version, or a first frame that does not decode
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Err ProtocolMismatch)
        Listener->>Listener: stop, the connection closes
        Client->>Client: ClientEvent::RegistrationRefused(code, reason)
    else the serial is in the revoked set
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Err Revoked)
        Listener->>Listener: stop, the connection closes
        Client->>Client: ClientEvent::RegistrationRefused(code, reason)
    else registers
        Listener->>Broker: RegistrationRequest(client_id, registration_id, identity, instance)
        Broker->>SM: RegistrationRequest
        alt the broker is shutting down
            SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Err "Broker is shutting down")
            Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Err)
            Client->>Client: ClientEvent::RegistrationRefused(code, reason)
        else a new session
            SM->>SA: spawn SessionAgent(new registration_id)
            opt it is not an instance that lost its session and asks for it back
                SM->>SM: supersede what its identity and instance held
            end
            SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok id, the session's address)
            Listener->>SA: ConnectionOpened(client_id, control): bound to the connection
            Note over Listener,SA: Bound before the client is told, so a publish sent<br/>the moment it hears (a facade sends its whole outbox then) has a session to go to.
            Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok registration_id)
            Client->>Client: ClientEvent::Registered, the builder sends every subscription again<br/>and asks for its signed documents again
        end
    end
    Note right of Client: Each subscribe and publish is then decided at the Listener<br/>(broker/client_subscription, broker/client_publish).
